      "hints": [
        "Consider $f(x) = 2 - \\frac{5}{x+2}$ for domain $x > -2$.",
        "Since $x > -2 \\implies x + 2 > 0$, the fraction $\\frac{5}{x+2}$ is strictly positive.",
        "Deduce that $f(x) < 2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Analyze the behavior of $f(x) = 2 - \\frac{5}{x+2}$ on the domain $x > -2$:\n$$\\text{For } x > -2, \\quad x + 2 > 0 \\implies \\frac{5}{x+2} > 0$$\n$$2 - \\frac{5}{x+2} < 2$$",
        "State the range of $f$:\n$$f(x) < 2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y < 2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad (-\\infty, 2)$$"
