      "hints": [
        "Set $y = 2 - \\frac{5}{x+2}$ and rearrange to make $x$ the subject.",
        "Isolate the fraction: $\\frac{5}{x+2} = 2 - y \\implies x + 2 = \\frac{5}{2-y} \\implies x = \\frac{5}{2-y} - 2 = \\frac{2y+1}{2-y}$.",
        "Recall that the domain of $f^{-1}$ is the range of $f$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = f(x)$ and isolate the fraction:\n$$y = 2 - \\frac{5}{x + 2} \\implies \\frac{5}{x + 2} = 2 - y$$",
        "Multiply by $(x + 2)$ and divide by $(2 - y)$:\n$$x + 2 = \\frac{5}{2 - y} \\implies x = \\frac{5}{2 - y} - 2 = \\frac{5 - 2(2 - y)}{2 - y} = \\frac{2y + 1}{2 - y}$$",
        "Interchange variables to state the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{2x + 1}{2 - x} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{5}{2 - x} - 2$$",
        "State the domain of $f^{-1}$, which equals the range of $f$ found in (a):\n$$\\text{Domain of } f^{-1}: \\quad x < 2$$"
      ],
